From 24cac802510ae519a016bdd5133a05c1e6c05ff4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:31:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build 95 note 17: the patron saint chooser, reworked from the
 app's own pieces

His word, 2026-11-13: "patron saint chooser design needs a rework". It was
the generic searchable dropdown: bare names in the website's order, sorted
on the name after its "St.", so the apostles and prophets whose names begin
"Holy Apostle" or "The Prophet" stood together under H and T; opened over
the Language section and ran to the foot of the screen with the page's own
words under its last row; no saint had his picture.

Now one chooser wherever a patron is chosen: Settings, the profile tab, the
computer's Data tab, and the Community profile's editor, which had its own
copy of the dropdown (eight lines in its Patron saint field):

  - the house's Sheet, `fill`, so it is as tall as the screen the keyboard
    leaves (useVisibleFrame) and whole above the keys; Back, Escape, its
    scrim and its close button close it, in the house's motion, still with
    reduced motion;
  - the one SearchField standing still over the list: any part of a name or
    a known form (lib/saints/nameForms.ts), accents off, the saints whose own
    name begins with the letters first, the list at its top with each letter;
  - each saint as the Saints list draws him: SaintIcon (a new size, 48 by
    64), the house's plate for the 26 whose pictures wait on a permission,
    and his feast as the Saints cards write it;
  - sorted and lettered by his own name (lib/profile/patrons.ts, ownName):
    the Apostle John and the Forerunner under J, Andrew under A;
  - the reader's own saint lit as the language and translation sheets light
    theirs, and in view as it opens; the row shows the chosen saint with his
    picture, or the plate and "No patron saint chosen", at one height.

The saints come from the library in brief the app carries, less any the
website does not list (/api/saints/patrons): a test build talks to the main
web, which knows 162 of the 270 saints until the merge and refuses the rest.

Held by lib/profile/__tests__/patronChooser.test.ts (nine tests; on the old
code the two drawn ones fail on their claims and the rest cannot load the
list). Walked on the export with touch at 360, 390 and 412, keys up and
down: 50 checks. Held for his yes before it is pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VuYTwc2v9NZk2Rs1Z1TZ29
